     "native": null,
     "phonemic": null,
     "notes": "",
     "etymology": "<number>11083</number> <b>lúpyatē</b> 'is lost, is removed' TS. (<i>apalupyátē</i> 'perishes' AV., <i>lupyamāna</i>- 'bewildered' MaitrUp.). 2. <b>lumpáti</b> 'destroys' Hariv., 'steals' BhP., 'elides'  RVPrāt. 3. <b>lupta-</b> 'robbed of, lacking, lost, destroyed' MBh. 4. <b>lōpayati</b> 'neglects, infringes' MBh., 'eliminates' R. 5. <b>*lōpyate</b> 'disappears' (cf. <i>lṓpya</i>- 'concealed' VS.com. [√<smallcaps><a data-entry=\"r416\">lup</a></smallcaps>]",
